Pont 's second this year , an <ei24 affirmation> of statements by top executives that they <ei25 intend> to <ei26 increase> rewards to shareholders . \" We have n't <ei27 benefited> the shareholder as much as we <ei28 need> to , \" <ei29 said> Edgar Woolard Jr., Du Pont 's chairman and chief executive officer , in an <ei30 interview> several months before he <ei32 entered> his current position in April . The largest beneficiary will be Seagram Co., which owns about 23 % of Du Pont . A spokesman for Seagram , the Montreal wine and spirits concern controlled by the Bronfman family , <ei35 said> the company will <ei36 post> additional pretax <ei37 profit> of about $ 33 million a year because of the additional Du Pont dividends . Du Pont also <ei40 announced> <ei41 plans> for a 3-for-1 stock <ei42 split> , although the initial higher dividend will be <ei43 paid> on pre-split shares . Du Pont 's stock <ei44 rose> $ 2.50 a share to <ei45 close> at $ 117.375 in New York Stock Exchange composite trading yesterday . Seagram <ei47 closed> at $ 84.75 , up 12.5 cents a share in Big Board trading . <ei48 Leading> the gains for Du Pont in the latest quarter was its industrial products segment , where profit <ei50 soared> to $ 155 million from $ 99 million a year earlier . The company <ei52 benefited> from continued strong <ei53 demand> and higher selling prices for titanium dioxide , a white pigment used in paints , paper and plastics . James Fallon , a New Providence , N.J., marketing consultant to the chemicals industry , <ei54 says> Du Pont still <ei55 holds> an edge in making the pigment because the company <ei57 was> \" first in with the technology \" to lower costs . He <ei58 said> Du Pont <ei59 holds> about 23 % of the world-wide market , the largest single share , at a time when growing uses for the pigment have kept it in tight supply , although others are now adding low-cost production capacity . Profit <ei60 climbed> to $ 98 million from $ 71 million in the petroleum segment , as Du Pont 's Conoco Inc. oil company was <ei62 helped> by crude oil prices higher than a year ago and by higher natural gas prices and volume . In the diversifed businesses segment , which includes herbicides , profit <ei64 grew> to $ 64 million from $ 27 million . A spokesman <ei65 said> herbicide <ei66 use> in some areas of the U.S. was <ei67 delayed> earlier in the year by heavy <ei70 rains> , thus <ei72 increasing> sales in the third quarter . In the fibers segment , profit <ei74 rose> to $ 180 million from $ 155 million , a gain Du Pont <ei75 attributed> to higher <ei76 demand> in the U.S. for most textile products . Two segments <ei77 posted> lower <ei78 earnings> for the quarter . Profit from coal <ei80 fell> to $ 41 million from $ 58 million , partly because of a miners ' <ei82 strike> . And profit from polymers <ei83 dropped> to $ 107 million from $ 122 million amid what Du Pont called lower demand and selling prices in certain packaging and industrial markets . For the nine months , Du Pont <ei85 earned> $ 2 billion , or $ 8.46 a share , up 18 % from $ 1.69 billion , or $ 7.03 a share , a year earlier . Sales <ei87 increased> 10 % to $ 26.54 billion from $ 24.05 billion . The increased dividend will be <ei88 paid> Dec . 14 to holders of record Nov . 15 . The stock <ei91 split> , which is subject to holder <ei92 approval> , would be <ei93 paid> on a still unspecified date in January to holders of record Dec . 21 .", "gold": [["ei11", "causes", "ei9"], ["ei57", "causes", "ei55"], ["ei62", "causes", "ei60"], ["ei67", "causes", "ei72"], ["ei70", "causes", "ei67"], ["ei82", "causes", "ei80"], ["ei9", "causedby", "ei11"], ["ei55", "causedby", "ei57"], ["ei60", "causedby", "ei62"], ["ei72", "causedby", "ei67"], ["ei67", "causedby", "ei70"], ["ei80", "causedby", "ei82"]], "lang": "eng", "mentions": ["ei1", "ei3", "ei5", "ei6", "ei7", "ei8", "ei9", "ei11", "ei12", "ei13", "ei14", "ei15", "ei16", "ei17", "ei18", "ei20", "ei22", "ei24", "ei25", "ei26", "ei2